cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use Rampa in research, please cite it as below.
type: software
title: 'Rampa: accessibility checks beyond syntax'
version: 0.1.1
abstract: >-
  An open-source WCAG 2.2 accessibility checker that runs axe-core, then asks a
  language model, one success criterion at a time, about what rules cannot
  decide, and keeps a finding only when its evidence is verified on the page.
  Evaluated against the W3C ACT test cases and corrupted pairs.
authors:
  - given-names: Guilherme
    family-names: Santiago
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/guilhermebsantiago/rampa-cli
url: https://rampa.guilhermebs.com.br
keywords:
  - accessibility
  - WCAG
  - automated accessibility testing
  - axe-core
  - large language models
  - ACT rules
